  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "To start the year 202620262026 off, Chef made a resolution to exercise daily. He decided to do exactly XXX push-ups every day.\n\nIf he sticks to his resolution, how many push-ups will he do in the month of January?\n\nNote that the month of January has 313131 days.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first and only line of input will contain a single integer XXX, denoting the number of push-ups Chef does every day.\n\n\nOutput Format\nOutput a single integer: the number of push-ups Chef will do in January.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤X≤1001 \\leq X \\leq 1001≤X≤100"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5",
        "output": "155",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nDoing 555 push-ups every day, Chef will end up doing 5×31=1555\\times 31 = 1555×31=155 push-ups in January."
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "100",
        "output": "3100",
        "explanation": ""
      }
    ]
  },
